THIRD-PARTY LICENSES
====================

This file is generated by cargo-about from about.toml and about.hbs; do not
edit it by hand. Regenerate it with scripts/third-party-licenses (CI fails
when it is stale).

It has two parts. The first holds the notices of code ported or vendored into
unityrs from other projects (UnityPy and UnityPyBoost, liblz4, CPython's
standard library, Pillow, zlib, OpenBLAS under BSD-3-Clause and its
GotoBLAS2 code under BSD-2-Clause-Views), and the provenance of bundled
data; the notice of a new port is added to about.hbs, its licence to its
crate's, and the notice to the crate's own files (a LICENSE-* file, and a
NOTICE-* file for a text of ours its licence asks for), so that the crate's
package carries it with the code. The second holds the licence of every crate the
unityrs workspace builds, its own members included, grouped by licence
text. A crate offered under a choice of licences (such as "MIT OR
Apache-2.0") is listed under the one about.toml prefers. liblzma-sys is also
listed under 0BSD, the licence of the xz sources it vendors and compiles,
and unityrs-imageio under Zlib, the licence of the zlib it vendors and
compiles (twice: the vendored LICENSE, and its LICENSE-ZLIB, the same text).

